/-!
# A ring map is a directed colimit of finite type maps of finite type `ℤ`-algebras

Proof of Stacks 00QY. Let `R → S` be a ring map. Index by the pairs `p = (E, F)` of a finite
subset `E ⊆ R` and a finite subset `F ⊆ S`, ordered by inclusion in both entries; this is a
nonempty directed partial order. Let `R_p ⊆ R` be the `ℤ`-subalgebra generated by `E` and
`S_p ⊆ S` the `ℤ`-subalgebra generated by `F` together with the image of `E`, so that `R → S`
restricts to `R_p → S_p`. Each `R_p` is of finite type over `ℤ`, being generated by `E`, and
each `R_p → S_p` is of finite type, `S_p` being of finite type over `ℤ` and hence over `R_p`.
Every element of `R` lies in `R_{(\{x\}, ∅)}` and every element of `S` in `S_{(∅, \{y\})}`, so
the two families cover `R` and `S`, and a monotone family of subrings covering the ring exhibits
it as the colimit of its members. Colimits in an arrow category are computed in each entry, so
`R → S` is the colimit of the system `R_p → S_p`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FiniteTypeMaps.solution`: the statement of Tag 00QY.

## Implementation notes

The colimit is proved from the ground up, out of one algebraic lemma:
`Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FiniteTypeMaps.exists_unique_ringHom_of_covering` says that if a family
of subrings `A i ⊆ R`, monotone and indexed by a nonempty directed preorder, covers `R`, then a
compatible family of ring maps `A i → T` extends uniquely to `R → T`. It is stated for an arbitrary
type of subrings (`SetLike` plus `SubringClass`), so that it applies both to the subrings and to
the `ℤ`-subalgebras used here, and monotonicity is phrased on members rather than as `Monotone`, so
that no order instance on the subobject type is involved. This is the missing general lemma:
Mathlib has `Subalgebra.iSupLift`, the same statement for algebra maps out of a directed supremum
of subalgebras, but nothing for ring maps, and using the algebra version would mean carrying the
two `ℤ`-algebra structures on a `ℤ`-subalgebra (`Subalgebra.algebra` and `algebraInt`) through the
construction.

From it, `Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FiniteTypeMaps.isColimitCoconeOfMonotone` gives the colimit in
`CommRingCat`, and the colimit in `Arrow CommRingCat` is
`CategoryTheory.Comma.fstSndJointlyReflectColimit`: the two projections of a comma category jointly
reflect colimits.

Finite type of `R_p → S_p` is deduced, rather than proved by exhibiting generators, from finite
type of `S_p` over `ℤ` by `Algebra.FiniteType.of_restrictScalars_finiteType` along the tower
`ℤ → R_p → S_p`, which is a tower because a ring map is uniquely a map of `ℤ`-algebras.

## References

* [StacksProject 00QY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QY)
-/

open CategoryTheory Limits

namespace Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FiniteTypeMaps

/-! ### Gluing a ring map along a covering family of subrings -/

section Covering

variable {Λ : Type*} [Preorder Λ] {R T : Type*} [CommRing R] [NonAssocSemiring T]
  {σ : Type*} [SetLike σ R] [SubringClass σ R]

/-- A monotone family of subrings `A i` of `R`, indexed by a nonempty directed preorder and
covering `R`, presents `R` as a colimit: a family of ring maps `f i : A i → T` compatible with
the inclusions extends uniquely to a ring map `R → T`. -/
private theorem exists_unique_ringHom_of_covering [Nonempty Λ] [IsDirected Λ (· ≤ ·)]
    (A : Λ → σ) (hmono : ∀ ⦃i j : Λ⦄, i ≤ j → ∀ ⦃x : R⦄, x ∈ A i → x ∈ A j)
    (hcov : ∀ x : R, ∃ i, x ∈ A i) (f : ∀ i, ↥(A i) →+* T)
    (hf : ∀ ⦃i j : Λ⦄ (h : i ≤ j) (x : R) (hx : x ∈ A i), f j ⟨x, hmono h hx⟩ = f i ⟨x, hx⟩) :
    ∃! g : R →+* T, ∀ (i : Λ) (x : R) (hx : x ∈ A i), g x = f i ⟨x, hx⟩ := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ (i j : Λ) (x : R) (hi : x ∈ A i) (hj : x ∈ A j), f i ⟨x, hi⟩ = f j ⟨x, hj⟩ := by
    intro i j x hi hj
    obtain ⟨k, hik, hjk⟩ := directed_of (· ≤ ·) i j
    rw [← hf hik x hi, ← hf hjk x hj]
  set g : R → T := fun x => f (hcov x).choose ⟨x, (hcov x).choose_spec⟩
  have hgi : ∀ (i : Λ) (x : R) (hx : x ∈ A i), g x = f i ⟨x, hx⟩ := fun i x hx =>
    key _ i x (hcov x).choose_spec hx
  have hpair : ∀ x y : R, ∃ k, x ∈ A k ∧ y ∈ A k := by
    intro x y
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hcov x
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hcov y
    obtain ⟨k, hik, hjk⟩ := directed_of (· ≤ ·) i j
    exact ⟨k, hmono hik hi, hmono hjk hj⟩
  have hmul : ∀ x y : R, g (x * y) = g x * g y := by
    intro x y
    obtain ⟨k, hx, hy⟩ := hpair x y
    rw [hgi k x hx, hgi k y hy, hgi k (x * y) (mul_mem hx hy)]
    exact map_mul (f k) ⟨x, hx⟩ ⟨y, hy⟩
  have hadd : ∀ x y : R, g (x + y) = g x + g y := by
    intro x y
    obtain ⟨k, hx, hy⟩ := hpair x y
    rw [hgi k x hx, hgi k y hy, hgi k (x + y) (add_mem hx hy)]
    exact map_add (f k) ⟨x, hx⟩ ⟨y, hy⟩
  refine ⟨{ toFun := g, map_one' := ?_, map_mul' := hmul, map_zero' := ?_, map_add' := hadd },
    hgi, ?_⟩
  · rw [hgi (Classical.arbitrary Λ) 1 (one_mem _)]
    exact map_one _
  · rw [hgi (Classical.arbitrary Λ) 0 (zero_mem _)]
    exact map_zero _
  · intro g' hg'
    ext x
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hcov x
    exact (hg' i x hi).trans (hgi i x hi).symm

end Covering

/-! ### The colimit of a covering family of subrings, in `CommRingCat` -/

section Diagram

variable {Λ : Type u} [Preorder Λ] {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {σ : Type*} [SetLike σ R]
  [SubringClass σ R] (A : Λ → σ)
  (hmono : ∀ ⦃i j : Λ⦄, i ≤ j → ∀ ⦃x : R⦄, x ∈ A i → x ∈ A j)

/-- The diagram of commutative rings given by a monotone family of subrings of `R` and the
inclusions between its members. -/
private def diagramOfMonotone : Λ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj i := CommRingCat.of ↥(A i)
  map {i j} h := CommRingCat.ofHom
    { toFun := fun x => ⟨x.1, hmono h.le x.2⟩
      map_one' := rfl
      map_mul' := fun _ _ => rfl
      map_zero' := rfl
      map_add' := fun _ _ => rfl }
  map_id i := by ext x; rfl
  map_comp f g := by ext x; rfl

/-- The cocone on `diagramOfMonotone` given by the inclusions of the members of the family
into `R`. -/
private def coconeOfMonotone : Cocone (diagramOfMonotone A hmono) where
  pt := CommRingCat.of R
  ι :=
    { app := fun i => CommRingCat.ofHom (SubringClass.subtype (A i))
      naturality := fun i j h => by ext x; rfl }

/-- A monotone family of subrings indexed by a nonempty directed preorder and covering the ring
exhibits the ring as the colimit of its members. -/
private noncomputable def isColimitCoconeOfMonotone [Nonempty Λ] [IsDirected Λ (· ≤ ·)]
    (hcov : ∀ x : R, ∃ i, x ∈ A i) : IsColimit (coconeOfMonotone A hmono) := by
  refine IsColimit.ofExistsUnique fun s => ?_
  obtain ⟨f, hfapp⟩ :
      ∃ f : ∀ i, ↥(A i) →+* ↥s.pt, ∀ (i : Λ) (x : ↥(A i)), f i x = (s.ι.app i).hom x :=
    ⟨fun i => (s.ι.app i).hom, fun _ _ => rfl⟩
  have hs : ∀ ⦃i j : Λ⦄ (h : i ≤ j) (x : R) (hx : x ∈ A i),
      f j ⟨x, hmono h hx⟩ = f i ⟨x, hx⟩ := by
    intro i j h x hx
    simp only [hfapp]
    exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (s.w (homOfLE h)) ⟨x, hx⟩
  obtain ⟨g, hg, huniq⟩ := exists_unique_ringHom_of_covering A hmono hcov f hs
  refine ⟨CommRingCat.ofHom g, fun j => ?_, fun l hl => ?_⟩
  · ext x
    change g x.1 = (s.ι.app j).hom x
    exact (hg j x.1 x.2).trans (hfapp j x)
  · refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (huniq l.hom fun i x hx => ?_)
    simp only [hfapp]
    exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (hl i) ⟨x, hx⟩

end Diagram

/-! ### The approximating system of a ring map -/

section Construction

variable {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S)

/-- The `ℤ`-subalgebra of `R` generated by a finite subset. -/
private def srcSub (E : Finset R) : Subalgebra ℤ R := Algebra.adjoin ℤ (E : Set R)

/-- The `ℤ`-subalgebra of `S` generated by a finite subset together with the image under `φ` of a
finite subset of `R`. -/
private def tgtSub (E : Finset R) (F : Finset S) : Subalgebra ℤ S :=
  Algebra.adjoin ℤ ((F : Set S) ∪ φ '' (E : Set R))

private lemma srcSub_mono {E E' : Finset R} (h : E ≤ E') {x : R} (hx : x ∈ srcSub E) :
    x ∈ srcSub E' :=
  Algebra.adjoin_mono (Finset.coe_subset.2 h) hx

private lemma tgtSub_mono {E E' : Finset R} {F F' : Finset S} (h : E ≤ E') (h' : F ≤ F')
    {y : S} (hy : y ∈ tgtSub φ E F) : y ∈ tgtSub φ E' F' :=
  Algebra.adjoin_mono
    (Set.union_subset_union (Finset.coe_subset.2 h') (Set.image_mono (Finset.coe_subset.2 h)))
    hy

private lemma exists_mem_srcSub (x : R) : x ∈ srcSub ({x} : Finset R) :=
  Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)

private lemma exists_mem_tgtSub (y : S) : y ∈ tgtSub φ (∅ : Finset R) ({y} : Finset S) :=
  Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_union_left _ (by simp))

private lemma map_mem_tgtSub (E : Finset R) (F : Finset S) :
    ∀ x ∈ srcSub E, φ x ∈ tgtSub φ E F := by
  intro x hx
  have h : srcSub E ≤ (tgtSub φ E F).comap φ.toIntAlgHom :=
    Algebra.adjoin_le fun y hy => Algebra.subset_adjoin (Set.mem_union_right _ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩)
  exact h hx

/-- The restriction of `φ` to the members of the approximating system. -/
private def mapAB (E : Finset R) (F : Finset S) : ↥(srcSub E) →+* ↥(tgtSub φ E F) :=
  φ.restrict _ _ (map_mem_tgtSub φ E F)

private lemma finiteType_srcSub (E : Finset R) : Algebra.FiniteType ℤ ↥(srcSub E) :=
  ⟨(Subalgebra.fg_top _).2 ⟨E, rfl⟩⟩

private lemma finiteType_tgtSub (E : Finset R) (F : Finset S) :
    Algebra.FiniteType ℤ ↥(tgtSub φ E F) := by
  have hfin : ((F : Set S) ∪ φ '' (E : Set R)).Finite :=
    F.finite_toSet.union (E.finite_toSet.image φ)
  refine ⟨(Subalgebra.fg_top _).2 ⟨hfin.toFinset, ?_⟩⟩
  simp only [Set.Finite.coe_toFinset]
  rfl

private lemma finiteType_mapAB (E : Finset R) (F : Finset S) : (mapAB φ E F).FiniteType := by
  let _ : Algebra ↥(srcSub E) ↥(tgtSub φ E F) := (mapAB φ E F).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower ℤ ↥(srcSub E) ↥(tgtSub φ E F) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (RingHom.ext_int _ _)
  have := finiteType_tgtSub φ E F
  exact Algebra.FiniteType.of_restrictScalars_finiteType ℤ ↥(srcSub E) ↥(tgtSub φ E F)

end Construction

/-! ### The presentation -/

section Presentation

variable {Λ : Type u} [PartialOrder Λ] {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (φ : R →+* S)
  (A : Λ → Subalgebra ℤ R) (B : Λ → Subalgebra ℤ S)
  (hA : ∀ ⦃i j : Λ⦄, i ≤ j → ∀ ⦃x : R⦄, x ∈ A i → x ∈ A j)
  (hB : ∀ ⦃i j : Λ⦄, i ≤ j → ∀ ⦃y : S⦄, y ∈ B i → y ∈ B j)
  (hmap : ∀ i : Λ, ∀ x ∈ A i, φ x ∈ B i)

/-- The diagram of ring maps `A i → B i` obtained by restricting `φ` to a monotone family of
subalgebras of the source and one of the target. -/
private def arrowDiagram : Λ ⥤ Arrow CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj i := Arrow.mk (CommRingCat.ofHom (φ.restrict (A i) (B i) (hmap i)))
  map {i j} h :=
    Arrow.homMk ((diagramOfMonotone A hA).map h) ((diagramOfMonotone B hB).map h) (by ext x; rfl)
  map_id i := Arrow.hom_ext _ _ (by ext x; rfl) (by ext x; rfl)
  map_comp f g := Arrow.hom_ext _ _ (by ext x; rfl) (by ext x; rfl)

/-- The cocone on `arrowDiagram` with tip `φ`, given by the inclusions of the members of the two
families. -/
private def arrowCocone : Cocone (arrowDiagram φ A B hA hB hmap) where
  pt := Arrow.mk (CommRingCat.ofHom φ)
  ι :=
    { app := fun i =>
        Arrow.homMk (CommRingCat.ofHom (SubringClass.subtype (A i)))
          (CommRingCat.ofHom (SubringClass.subtype (B i))) (by ext x; rfl)
      naturality := fun i j h => Arrow.hom_ext _ _ (by ext x; rfl) (by ext x; rfl) }

/-- If the two families cover the source and the target, the ring map `φ` is the colimit of the
system of its restrictions: colimits in the arrow category are computed in each entry. -/
private noncomputable def colimitPresentationOfCovering [Nonempty Λ] [IsDirected Λ (· ≤ ·)]
    (hcovA : ∀ x : R, ∃ i, x ∈ A i) (hcovB : ∀ y : S, ∃ i, y ∈ B i) :
    ColimitPresentation Λ (Arrow.mk (CommRingCat.ofHom φ)) where
  diag := arrowDiagram φ A B hA hB hmap
  ι := (arrowCocone φ A B hA hB hmap).ι
  isColimit :=
    Comma.fstSndJointlyReflectColimit (isColimitCoconeOfMonotone A hA hcovA)
      (isColimitCoconeOfMonotone B hB hcovB)

end Presentation

private lemma isDirected_prod_finset (R S : Type u) :
    IsDirected (Finset R × Finset S) (· ≤ ·) := by
  classical
  refine ⟨fun p q => ⟨(p.1 ∪ q.1, p.2 ∪ q.2), ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩⟩ <;>
    simp [Finset.subset_union_left, Finset.subset_union_right]

/-- **A ring map is a directed colimit of finite type ring maps between `ℤ`-algebras of finite
type** (Stacks 00QY). -/
public theorem solution (X : Arrow CommRingCat.{u}) :
    ∃ (Λ : Type u) (_ : PartialOrder Λ) (_ : IsDirected Λ (· ≤ ·)) (_ : Nonempty Λ)
      (pres : ColimitPresentation Λ X), ∀ i : Λ,
        Algebra.FiniteType ℤ (pres.diag.obj i).left ∧ (pres.diag.obj i).hom.hom.FiniteType := by
  have hdir := isDirected_prod_finset ↥X.left ↥X.right
  refine ⟨Finset ↥X.left × Finset ↥X.right, inferInstance,
    hdir, inferInstance,
    colimitPresentationOfCovering X.hom.hom (fun p => srcSub p.1)
      (fun p => tgtSub X.hom.hom p.1 p.2) (fun _ _ h _ hx => srcSub_mono h.1 hx)
      (fun _ _ h _ hy => tgtSub_mono X.hom.hom h.1 h.2 hy)
      (fun p => map_mem_tgtSub X.hom.hom p.1 p.2)
      (fun x => ⟨({x}, ∅), exists_mem_srcSub x⟩)
      (fun y => ⟨(∅, {y}), exists_mem_tgtSub X.hom.hom y⟩),
    fun p => ⟨finiteType_srcSub p.1, finiteType_mapAB X.hom.hom p.1 p.2⟩⟩

end Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FiniteTypeMaps

/-!
# A ring map is a directed colimit of finite type maps of finite type `ℤ`-algebras

Let `R → S` be an arbitrary ring map. Then there are a directed poset `Λ`, a system of ring
maps `R_λ → S_λ` indexed by `Λ`, and maps making `R → S` the colimit of that system, such that
each `R_λ` is of finite type over `ℤ` and each `S_λ` is of finite type over `R_λ`.

The witness is the absolute one: `Λ` is the poset of pairs `(E, F)` of finite subsets `E ⊆ R`
and `F ⊆ S`, with `R_λ ⊆ R` the `ℤ`-subalgebra generated by `E` and `S_λ ⊆ S` the
`ℤ`-subalgebra generated by `F` and the image of `E`. Every element of `R` lies in some `R_λ`
and every element of `S` in some `S_λ`, so the directed unions are `R` and `S`.

## Main results

* `CommRingCat.exists_colimitPresentation_arrow_finiteType`: a ring map, viewed as an object of
  the arrow category of `CommRingCat`, is a colimit over a nonempty directed poset of a diagram
  of ring maps `R_λ → S_λ` with `R_λ` of finite type over `ℤ` and `R_λ → S_λ` of finite type.

## Implementation notes

A ring map is an object `X : Arrow CommRingCat`, with source `X.left`, target `X.right` and
structure map `X.hom`; a morphism of `Arrow CommRingCat` is a commuting square, so a diagram
`Λ ⥤ Arrow CommRingCat` is exactly the source's system of ring maps `R_λ → S_λ` together with
its transition squares. Item (1) of the source, "the colimit of the system is `R → S`", is the
bundled `Limits.ColimitPresentation Λ X`: a diagram, a cocone on it with tip `X`, and the
assertion that this cocone is colimiting. Colimits in an arrow category are computed in each
entry, so this says both `colim R_λ = R` and `colim S_λ = S`, compatibly with the structure maps.

Items (2) and (3) are the ring-theoretic `Algebra.FiniteType ℤ R_λ` and `RingHom.FiniteType` of
`R_λ → S_λ`, as in Lemmas `00QO` and `0BUF`. They could equivalently be stated as
`Algebra.FiniteType ℤ R_λ ∧ Algebra.FiniteType ℤ S_λ`, because a `ℤ`-algebra of finite type is
of finite type over any intermediate ring and conversely finite type composes; the source's
relative form is kept, being the one item (3) states and the one that survives when `ℤ` is
replaced by another base. As `ℤ` is Noetherian, finite type over `ℤ` agrees with finite
presentation over `ℤ` (`Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType`), and then `R_λ → S_λ` is of
finite presentation as well, so the diagram consists of finitely presented arrows automatically;
nothing is lost by phrasing the conditions with finite type, as the source does.

The index category is the source's own: a nonempty directed partial order in the same universe,
rather than merely a small filtered category. That is the stronger of the two readings and it is
what the construction above produces. Mathlib's idiom for "is a filtered colimit of objects with
property `P`" is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.ind P`, and this statement implies that form in
one step, a nonempty directed poset being filtered, via
`ObjectProperty.of_essentiallySmall_index`; the converse needs the cofinality theorem that every
filtered colimit is a colimit over a directed poset, so `ind` is a consequence here rather than
the content.

Faithfulness. (1) No hypothesis is dead: there is no hypothesis beyond the ring map `X` itself,
which the conclusion is about, and the source likewise assumes nothing of `R → S`. (2) The
scalars and bases are the source's: `Algebra.FiniteType ℤ` is over the initial ring `ℤ`, and
finite type of `R_λ → S_λ` is over `R_λ`, not over `ℤ` and not over `R`. (3) The comparison maps
are pinned, not merely asserted to exist: `ColimitPresentation` carries the cocone
`ι : diag ⟶ (const Λ).obj X`, so the maps `R_λ → R` and `S_λ → S` are given and are compatible
with the structure maps, and `isColimit` says they exhibit `R → S` as the colimit. (4) The
instantiation is not degenerate: for `X` the identity of `ℤ` a one-point diagram works, whereas
for `X = (ℝ → ℝ[T])` no term of any such diagram can be `X`, since `ℝ` is not of finite type
over `ℤ`; so the statement asserts the existence of a genuinely infinite approximating system.

## References

* [StacksProject 00QY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QY)

## Tags

directed colimit, finite type, ring map, arrow category
-/

open CategoryTheory Limits

namespace CommRingCat

/-- **A ring map is a directed colimit of finite type ring maps between `ℤ`-algebras of finite
type.** Given a ring map `X : R ⟶ S`, there are a nonempty directed poset `Λ` and a diagram of
ring maps `R_λ ⟶ S_λ` over `Λ`, together with a colimit cocone exhibiting `R ⟶ S` as its
colimit, such that each `R_λ` is of finite type over `ℤ` and each `R_λ ⟶ S_λ` is of finite
type. -/
@[stacks 00QY "A ring map is an object of `Arrow CommRingCat`, and the source's item (1) is the
bundled `Limits.ColimitPresentation Λ X` (diagram, cocone, colimiting), colimits in an arrow
category being computed entrywise. The index is the source's nonempty directed poset; Mathlib's
`ObjectProperty.ind` form follows from this one. See the module docstring."]
public theorem exists_colimitPresentation_arrow_finiteType (X : Arrow CommRingCat.{u}) :
    ∃ (Λ : Type u) (_ : PartialOrder Λ) (_ : IsDirected Λ (· ≤ ·)) (_ : Nonempty Λ)
      (pres : ColimitPresentation Λ X), ∀ i : Λ,
        Algebra.FiniteType ℤ (pres.diag.obj i).left ∧ (pres.diag.obj i).hom.hom.FiniteType :=
  Stacks.ColimitPresentation.FiniteTypeMaps.solution X

end CommRingCat
